--
N5008 [over.match.best] + [over.ics.user] + [temp.deduct]: a user-defined
conversion via a (templated, SFINAE-guarded) converting constructor is viable
based only on the source and destination types, not on the scope of the call
site.  CBMC wrongly rejects `std::filesystem::remove(name)` (name : std::string)
with "found no match for symbol 'remove'" -> CONVERSION ERROR whenever the call
appears inside an OUT-OF-LINE, qualified function definition (class member,
namespace member, or static member); the identical call in a free function at
namespace scope resolves fine.  The distinguishing factor is that the current
scope during overload resolution is a nested (out-of-line-definition) scope, in
which the std::string->std::filesystem::path converting-constructor template
fails to resolve.

Faithful reproducer, reduced from src/util/tempfile.cpp
(`temporary_filet::~temporary_filet`) via cvise while keeping the real
<string>/<filesystem> includes (so libstdc++ stays semantically faithful).
Reproduces the dog-food FAIL for tempfile.cpp.  assertion.2 provides
non-vacuity.  Flip to CORE once the converting-constructor conversion resolves
independently of the call-site scope.
